1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:12,590
Slide 21 provides our "OPERATIONAL PREREQUISITES CHECKLIST: Before You Launch." James, Sarah, what are the three non-negotiable launch gates?

2
00:00:13,490 --> 00:00:15,422
Gate 1: Environment Secrets!

3
00:00:15,422 --> 00:00:22,531
If I see a student hardcoding an API key into a Python file, I will fail their code review immediately!

4
00:00:22,531 --> 00:00:29,090
All secrets must live in `.env`, excluded in `.gitignore`, and guarded by git pre-commit hooks!

5
00:00:29,990 --> 00:00:32,135
Gate 2: Database Migration.

6
00:00:32,135 --> 00:00:45,090
Ensure your SQLite relational tables for `tasks`, `memory_embeddings`, `audit_logs`, and `ap2_mandates` are initialized and indexed before running background jobs!

7
00:00:45,990 --> 00:00:48,116
And Gate 3: AP2 Spending Caps!

8
00:00:48,116 --> 00:00:57,970
Never connect a payment tool without setting hard limits—like a maximum of $50 per transaction and $200 per day—locked at the kernel level!

9
00:00:58,870 --> 00:01:05,520
When all three gates are verified green, your system is hardened against 99% of production accidents!

10
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:12,350
Now let us examine our second major enterprise case study on Slide 22!

